00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:30.980
episode

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:30.980
"The
\hSilk Dress
\hand the Ragged Dress"

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:45.410
Oscar!

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:47.420
It's been decided!

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:50.120
His Majesty has given his permission, Oscar!

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.830
I'm finally going to Paris, aren't I?

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.630
I can hardly wait for next week to come!

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.100
Say, tell me, Oscar!

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:01.670
Is it really true the Champs-Élysées
promenade is made of marble?

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.170
Are there really ghosts in the Notre Dame towers?

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:04.640
Tell me!

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.470
Dauphine, your visit to Paris is not for pleasure.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:10.500
Of course I know that, Oscar.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:14.170
But I can't control the excitement in my heart!

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:16.010
Your Highness.

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:18.480
This is a ceremony for the future
King and his royal wife,

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.070
to greet and make themselves
familiar to the people of Paris.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.420
Yes, don't worry.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.320
I'll do a fine job!

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:28.490
Oh, but my heart is fluttering
in excitement already!

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:29.930
Paris!

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:31.290
The City of Flowers, Paris!

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:35.130
Say, Oscar, what dress should I wear?

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.870
Oh, that's right! Which crown? Which ribbons?

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:40.090
What about earrings?

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:43.140
It's like a dream!

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.940
My longing! My Paris!

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:47.350
My Paris! My Paris!!

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:48.970
My Paris! My Paris!!

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:03.500
It's hard to believe she's the same age as you.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:04.660
Who?

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.600
You and the Dauphine.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.060
She doesn't seem like she's 17, at all.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:09.120
She's like a child.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:11.670
Is that supposed to be a compliment towards me?

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:12.500
Don't be silly!

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.420
Why would I compliment you?

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:19.770
Still, I adore Lady Antoinette's child-like spirit.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.880
She possesses such noble pride and dignity,

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.750
yet she's immediately attracted
to strength and beauty.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:28.780
She follows where her emotions take her,
and that's what I adore about her.

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:30.620
I see.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:33.270
So people are attracted to what they don't have.

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:35.390
Perhaps you're right.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:37.230
She does have her shortcomings, as well.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:43.030
Still, it's impossible for anyone to not like Lady
Antoinette's character, after being by her side.

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:45.300
You feel the same way, don't you?

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.270
Yeah.

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:50.500
I'm not so sure of the part about
everyone liking her though...

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:15.800
That Austrian brat is really letting
things go to her head, isn't she?

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:18.670
If she becomes popular with the people,

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:22.070
it means the popularity of the
Dauphin will increase, as well!

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:24.170
That damn dimwitted locksmith!

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:33.330
Anyhow, for those of us who wish to see you
become the next king, this doesn't sit well{ with us}!

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:36.590
I hope you have already come
up with some kind of plan?

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:39.190
There is a man who holds a grudge
against the Royal Guards,

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:42.840
and a rather interesting event is
being planned for their Paris visit...

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:48.920
If the reputation of both the royal couple
and that impudent Oscar become ruined...!

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:51.430
Killing two birds with one stone, I see...

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:26.740
The Royal Guards are so dashing!

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:27.110
So wonderful!

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:28.240
But what are they doing in Paris?

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.410
Lady Antoinette must be coming to Paris!
They're probably preparing for her visit!

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:33.050
Lady Antoinette?!

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:35.050
I'll have to come and see her!

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:37.280
That area is the eleventh district.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.050
There's no need to see the inner-city areas,

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:41.180
as they have nothing to do with the parade route.

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:53.610
<i>In the Palace of Versailles,
the nobility lived in opulence.</i>

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.530
<i>This is twenty kilometers to the west.</i>

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:59.140
<i>Here in Paris, the City of Flowers,</i>

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:02.760
<i>the people were suffering from
the presence of a bad government.</i>

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:09.580
<i>Especially in the poor districts,
such as Temple and Gravilliers,</i>

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:14.710
<i>the people weren't able to find any work
and were living in crushing poverty.</i>

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:30.400
Thief!

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:31.270
It's a thief!

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:32.740
Somebody catch him!

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:33.400
Come back here!

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:35.110
Now's our chance!

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:36.540
Bread!

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:49.120
~ The Princess is coming, ~

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:51.220
~ in her golden carriage. ~

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:52.840
~ The Princess is coming, ~

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:55.260
~ in her golden carriage. ~

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.300
~ The Princess is coming, ~

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.360
~ in her golden car—

00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:59.360
Shut up!

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:00.400
Scram!

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.760
It's mean Jeanne!

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:20.420
Potato soup again!

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:21.990
Stop fooling around already...

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.330
...and deliver the finished
laundry to Malcombe's shop for me.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.130
I don't want to.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:29.090
Listen to you...

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:31.670
Why can't you be more like Rosalie?

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:33.460
Well, too bad.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:36.590
I'm not obedient like Rosalie.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:41.740
Hey, Mom!

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:45.560
Is it true our father was the
last noble of the Valois family?

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.020
Good grief, that story again?

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:49.380
Think about it!

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:52.350
The lineage of the Valois family
traces back to the Valois Dynasty,

00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:55.020
which ruled before the
current Bourbon Dynasty!

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:58.490
Rosalie and I are the last ones
alive from that family, right?

00:09:58.720 --> 00:09:59.870
Back then,

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:04.230
I was a maid for the Valois family,
while they were facing ruin.

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:06.530
The Master graciously loved me.

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:09.130
And that's how Rosalie and I were born.

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:10.330
Yes,

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:13.970
but soon after Rosalie was born,
the Master passed away,

00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:17.560
and that was the end of
the poor Valois family.

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:23.810
If they had stayed in power, we would
be living in Versailles now!

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:24.890
Right, Rosalie?

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:27.020
Versailles? Don't be silly.

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:28.850
Oh, Jeanne, you and your dreams!

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.150
A dream?

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:33.160
No, it's not a dream! It's not!

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:36.340
It's our lives now that are a dream!

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:38.630
It's a nightmare! A nightmare!

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:40.160
Washed-out, faded dresses!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.370
Mud-stained shoes!

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:44.870
We live in this hog pen of a house,
in this garbage dump we call a city!

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:49.300
Day after day, all we eat is cracked
barley bread and potato soup!

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:53.140
Mom...!

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:55.510
You won't work,

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:58.450
but you'll keep saying such things
while staring at the mirror everyday?!

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:00.890
You're 17 already!

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:04.270
You can work as a seamstress
or a maid, or do whatever!

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:09.490
If I were healthier, I'd work myself to the bone,

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:11.930
so I could buy nice dresses for you two!

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:13.810
So I could feed you better food!

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:17.690
Mom!

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:21.910
You have no idea how
painful it is for me, yet you...

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:23.780
I've had enough of your sob stories!

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:24.700
Jeanne!

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:28.850
I'll climb my way out of this
place with my own hands!

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:32.580
When opportunity comes, I'll seize it and I swear,
I'll wear a silk dress with lace someday!

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:34.150
Jeanne!

00:11:34.150 --> 00:11:34.980
Rosalie.

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.320
Just let her be.

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:40.790
She'll come home when she's hungry.

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:42.220
Are you okay, Mom?

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:44.200
Thank you.

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.160
You're a kind child, Rosalie.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:49.870
Rosalie, you have no idea how fortunate
I am to have you by my side.

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:51.940
Of course I'd be by your side.

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.440
I'm your daughter.

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:58.010
Of course... You're my daughter...!

00:11:58.010 --> 00:11:59.860
My precious, precious daughter!

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:25.430
Isn't that... Duke de Guéméné?

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.080
It looks like he's here incognito.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:32.480
That's...!

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:33.680
The other man...!

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:34.650
Do you know him?

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:37.150
He was a member of the
Royal Guards until a year ago.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:39.320
His name is Charles Corday.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:42.290
He's a fearsomely skilled
swordsman and also clever,

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:44.570
but gambling changed him for the worse
and he was dismissed from the Guards.

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:47.660
But why would Charles be with de Guéméné...?

00:13:03.310 --> 00:13:05.640
Oh, merciful Sir!

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:09.350
Please have mercy on this poor soul,
who is from the Valois family lineage!

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:10.890
Get away from me, you beggar!

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:15.240
Go!

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:20.890
Stingy bastard!

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:22.420
Old fart! Jerk!

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:24.820
Ow...

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:28.760
Damn!

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:32.700
<i>The nobility, the rich... We're all human!</i>

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:37.000
<i>Just because I lost out on my birth,
doesn't mean I have to accept it!</i>

00:13:53.590 --> 00:13:57.860
Thank goodness the Princess came all the way
from Austria and married the Dauphin.

00:13:57.860 --> 00:13:59.940
We were able to avoid a war thanks to her.

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:01.370
That's right.

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:05.900
From now on taxes will be lower
and life will only get better.

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:07.400
We all have to give her a warm welcome.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:15.330
An officer has just returned from Paris.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.520
Apparently, the city is packed
with people like never before.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:19.300
Make sure you stay alert.

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:19.710
Yes.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:24.200
Vigilantly watch the parade route ahead of you
and pay close attention to the horses' demeanor.

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:26.140
If the people get too excited,

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:28.430
there's no guarantee that the
horses won't get frightened.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:29.670
I understand.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:35.680
Perhaps I am getting old, André.

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:37.080
Why do you suddenly say so?

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:39.780
I can't help but feel something
terrible might happen...

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:42.380
I just hope Oscar fulfills
her duty without any trouble...

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:50.990
Forward!

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:06.980
Commander, do you remember that man,
Charles, we saw the other day?

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:08.880
The man who was with du Guéméné?

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:10.150
Yes, that's right.

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:11.820
I looked into it,

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:14.640
and learned he has been frequently
visiting a gunpowder mill.

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:16.480
A gunpowder mill?!

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.370
It's a fool-proof plan.

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:32.200
Loud sounds and sparks will
go off one after another.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.530
The horses will go wild no matter
how well-trained they are.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:35.470
The location?

00:15:35.470 --> 00:15:37.160
Leave everything to me.

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:43.750
<i>On this day,</i>

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:47.580
<i>the sky above Paris was clear
without a single cloud in sight.</i>

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:53.060
<i>The 18-year-old Dauphin and
the 17-year-old Dauphine,</i>

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:57.760
<i>had officially visited the capital city
of Paris for the first time.</i>

00:15:57.760 --> 00:15:58.860
Look at her!

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:01.300
The Dauphine looks like she
stepped out of a painting!

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:03.200
If someone like her becomes Queen,

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:05.900
I'm sure life will get better
and we can live happily.

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:08.730
That's right! It has to turn out that way,
or it'll be nothing but a cruel joke!

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:13.110
Your Highness, the people are delighted
by our visit, aren't they?

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:13.740
Yes.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.050
So many...

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:17.340
So many people are welcoming us!

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:31.990
Stop! Where are you going?!

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:35.230
I have an urgent message for the
Commander of the Royal Guards!

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:36.050
Please let me through!

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:37.330
That's impossible!

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:39.260
The Commander is positioned
beside the Dauphin's carriage!

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:41.980
There's reason to believe firecrackers
might be thrown into the carriage!

00:16:42.340 --> 00:16:43.140
What?!

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:49.820
Oscar.

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:52.180
André?

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:54.060
What are you doing here—?

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:54.070
Shh! Give me your ear!

00:16:56.420 --> 00:16:57.180
What?!

00:16:58.320 --> 00:16:59.720
Girodelle, take charge here!

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:01.700
Commander...?!

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:06.460
André! You search the left side!

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:43.020
Stop!

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:34.550
Speak! Duke de Guéméné hired you, didn't he?

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:38.820
You were once a member of the Royal Guards.

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:40.930
How dare you endanger the Dauphin!

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:41.970
Shame on you!

00:18:55.910 --> 00:18:57.670
He came prepared with poison...!

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:15.130
It's absolutely magnificent, Oscar!

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.880
To think that so many people love me!

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:21.790
I am truly blessed!

00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:32.740
<i>If Antoinette had never forgotten the happiness
and love she felt on this day,</i>

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:38.610
<i>perhaps she wouldn't have had
to become such a tragic Queen.</i>

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:46.720
Who cares about the stupid Dauphin!

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.720
Who cares about ''our dear Queen!''

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:57.330
That's a pretty nice carriage.

00:19:57.330 --> 00:19:58.970
Guess I'll give it a try.

00:19:58.970 --> 00:20:00.170
Please stop! Please stop!!

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:01.260
Please stop! Please stop!!

00:20:04.710 --> 00:20:06.680
You idiot! Don't jump out suddenly!

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:07.350
What is the matter?

00:20:07.710 --> 00:20:10.010
Madame! Kind Madame!

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:13.810
Please have mercy on this poor orphan,
who is from the Valois family lineage!

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:15.440
The Valois family, did you say?!

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:16.400
Yes.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:19.460
I've heard the rumors that the Valois
family is survived by a child, but...

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:22.360
Yes, my father's name is Baron Saint-Rémy.

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:23.660
Saint-Rémy?!

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:25.820
I knew that Saint-Rémy well!

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:27.560
My father and mother are dead,

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:30.300
and without any fortune or family to depend on,

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:31.790
I'm all alone...

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:33.570
Poor thing...

00:20:33.570 --> 00:20:36.170
The descendant of the royal
House of Valois in such plight...

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:37.170
Here, come in.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:44.300
I am Marquise Boulainvilliers.

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:47.150
You must tell me everything at my manor.

00:20:47.150 --> 00:20:47.770
Madame...

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:53.990
This is my chance!

00:20:53.990 --> 00:20:55.230
My dream will finally come true!

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:57.330
I can live the life I deserve!

00:20:57.330 --> 00:20:59.690
I'll do anything for that!

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:00.900
Anything!

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:09.670
I'm sorry, but the price has gone
up to 15 centimes starting today.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:12.980
The price of meat and vegetables keep going up,

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:15.380
so we can't survive with what
we've been making anymore.

00:21:17.680 --> 00:21:21.720
<i>If we continue to buy bread, we won't have
enough to buy butter or Mom's medicine.</i>

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:22.950
<i>It's frightening...</i>

00:21:22.950 --> 00:21:24.800
<i>How are we going to survive from now on?</i>

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:28.490
<i>Jeanne!</i>

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:29.990
<i>Please come home!</i>

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:31.350
<i>Help me!</i>

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:37.060
Are you all right, Mademoiselle?

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:39.640
Yes, I'm all right.

00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:41.980
It's my own fault for walking absentmindedly.

00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:44.070
Excuse me then.

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:53.320
Compared to the main boulevard, the lives of
\h the people in this area are terrible, aren't they?

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:54.330
Indeed.

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:57.890
They avoided a war by arranging a
union with the House of Habsburg,

00:21:57.890 --> 00:22:02.300
but the King is apparently unaware that a great number of his people are on the brink of starvation.

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:04.590
<i>Just what will happen to France?</i>

00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:08.670
<i>After studying weaponry in Germany,</i>

00:22:08.670 --> 00:22:10.370
<i>medicine in Italy,</i>

00:22:10.370 --> 00:22:14.330
<i>and philosophy in Switzerland,
the Swedish noble, Fersen,</i>

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:19.960
<i>has come to France to further refine
himself at the French court.</i>

00:22:19.960 --> 00:22:21.410
<i>Antoinette,</i>

00:22:21.410 --> 00:22:22.490
<i>Oscar,</i>

00:22:22.490 --> 00:22:25.980
<i>and Fersen's fateful encounter was drawing near.</i>

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:33.370
To be continued

